{
  "_comment": "Wave 1B canonical ingredient dictionary (independent-review Blocker 4, PRODUCTION_CATALOG_WAVE_1B_REAL_DATA.md). Reviewable, committed, operator-curated structured data -- NOT reconstructed ad hoc from every raw manifest string at runtime. One entry per distinct chemical identity that appears anywhere in catalog_data/production/wave1b/manifest.jsonl (as ingredient_details[].raw_name, the concentration-stripped clean identity -- see app.domain.catalog_source_adapter.IngredientDetail). Generated once, deterministically, by grouping the manifest's own distinct normalized (lowercase/whitespace-collapsed) ingredient identities and picking one representative spelling per group; reviewed and committed here rather than re-derived at import time. 'aliases' lists every OTHER verbatim raw spelling this exact chemical identity was disclosed under across the acquired products -- the only ingredient genuinely needing this is plain Water, disclosed three different ways across CeraVe ('AQUA / WATER / EAU', or 'WATER' alone on Drug Facts-labeled pages) and The Ordinary ('Aqua (Water)'); a botanical extract like 'Aloe Barbadensis Leaf Water' or 'Rosa Damascena Flower Water' is never folded into this group -- those are chemically distinct ingredients that merely share the word 'water'. Every other entry has an empty alias list: its one observed raw spelling (modulo case, which resolve_ingredient() already normalizes) is its own canonical name. 'ingredient_type'/'inci_name' are left null throughout -- this pass does not fabricate a taxonomic classification it was never given by the source; a later, separately-reviewed pass may fill these in deliberately. app/domain/catalog_wave1b_population.py is the ONLY code that reads this file, and it performs exact (never fuzzy) normalized-string matching against it -- an ingredient identity encountered during population that has NO entry here is left as an open, unresolved review item, never guessed.",
